   "fix": "New pure `lib/faceSeriesRanking.ts` ranks ONLY already-eligible series from de-identified signals: tier 0 T1-weighted; tier 1 unpenalized (T2/FLAIR/GRE/CT/unknown); tier 2 fat-suppressed (ScanOptions token FS or F/S/FATSAT/STIR/SPAIR/SPIR text); tier 3 diffusion (DWI/ADC/TRACE/TRACEW/DTI/EDC/diff) or localizer (SURVEY/SCOUT/LOCALIZER/TOPOGRAM/loc; CT ScanOptions SURVIEW/SCOUT/TOPOGRAM). Within a tier: voxel count desc (unknown last), then series_info.id asc, then input order. `resolveEligibility` pass 1 now filters eligible records and calls `selectFaceSeries`, which issues ONE bounded `sop_instances` aggregate (job_id + lead-tier UIDs, SUM CAST to BIGINT because /api/query nulls NUMERIC; instance_count fallback) only when >=2 series share the lead tier; geometry failure is non-fatal (scrubbed warn) and never changes eligibility. Rank signals (ProtocolName, ScanOptions, id) travel in a separate `FaceSeriesRecord.rank` and never reach the classifier's `meta`. The dead `dicom_elements` fallback keeps first-match order (table absent on the live backend). Classifier `lib/faceEligibility.ts` untouched.",
