  "raw": "---\nstatus: diagnosed\ntrigger: \"No audio on the SFU path. Camera connects but voice produces no audible audio.\"\ncreated: 2026-06-28T00:00:00Z\nupdated: 2026-06-28T00:00:00Z\n---\n\n## Current Focus\n\nhypothesis: CONFIRMED — remote audio track is consumed by the SDK but never attached to any audible DOM element (VideoTile drops audioTrack). Secondary: mic publish is skipped on first enable because `session` is null at call time.\ntest: traced full audio path mic -> produce -> SFU -> consume -> DOM across use-media.ts, VideoChatGrid.tsx, SDK dist, plus grep for any audio element in SFU path\nexpecting: no `<audio>` / `new Audio()` / `.play()` in SFU path -> confirmed\nnext_action: report ROOT CAUSE FOUND (find_root_cause_only mode — no fix)\n\n## Symptoms\n\nexpected: With NEXT_PUBLIC_FF_SFU_MEDIA=true, voice on SFU path produces audible audio — the other user hears the speaker\nactual: No audio on the SFU path. Camera connects and ICE reaches connected, but no audio is heard\nerrors: None reported\nreproduction: Two browsers, flag ON, mic enabled in one. Test 2 in 04-UAT.md\nstarted: SFU cutover (flag-gated path), Phase 04-04\n\n## Eliminated\n\n- hypothesis: Suspect #4 — SFU rejects audio producer (router rtpCapabilities lack audio codec / transport video-only)\n  evidence: SDK produce path is codec-agnostic (transport.produce({track}); kind derived from track). A produce rejection would throw from publishMic -> caught at use-media.ts:263 -> toast \"Microphone error\". Symptom reports NO errors. SDK consume path emits trackSubscribed(participantId, track, 'audio') generically (index.js:328). No evidence of audio-kind restriction.\n  timestamp: 2026-06-28\n\n- hypothesis: Suspect #3 — consumer attached but autoplay-blocked / muted element\n  evidence: There is NO media element wired for remote audio at all (no `<audio>`, audioTrack never added to any srcObject). It is not \"blocked from playing\"; it is never wired to play. Autoplay-block is therefore moot.\n  timestamp: 2026-06-28\n\n## Evidence\n\n- timestamp: 2026-06-28\n  checked: watch.sideby.me/src/features/room/components/VideoChatGrid.tsx VideoTile (lines 132-155, 167-181)\n  found: VideoTile receives `audioTrack` as a prop (passed at line 96) but NEVER destructures or uses it (destructure list lines 132-140 omits audioTrack). The only srcObject wiring builds a video-only stream: `new MediaStream([videoTrack])` (line 152). When the camera is off (`isOff`), no `<video>` is rendered at all — only an avatar div (lines 175-181). No `<audio>` element exists anywhere.\n  implication: The remote audio track is dropped at the DOM layer — never attached to an audible element, never played. Unconditional: holds regardless of camera state. Explains why video plays but audio never does.\n\n- timestamp: 2026-06-28\n  checked: SDK dist index.js (publishMic->publishTrack->produce at 445-448/249-261; consumeProducer at 311-328) and index.d.ts trackSubscribed signature (line 96)\n  found: SDK correctly produces audio (publishMic -> transport.produce({track}) with kind=audio) and consumes remote audio (transport.consume -> resume -> events.emit('trackSubscribed', participantId, track, 'audio')). Audio is produced/transported/consumed correctly at the SDK layer.\n  implication: The break is NOT in the SDK produce/consume. The chain delivers the audio track to the consumer; the failure is purely on the watch side at attach/playback (and conditionally at the publish call site — see next).\n\n- timestamp: 2026-06-28\n  checked: use-media.ts enableMic (lines 245-268) + SfuSession (SDK has no auto-republish of publishedTracks/localTracks on connect)\n  found: enableMic publishes only `if (session)` (line 260). On the FIRST enable, sdkEnabled is still false so useMediaRoom's session is null; enableMic's closure (deps [session]) captured session=null, so `session.publishMic(track)` is SKIPPED. setIsMicActive(true) only THEN flips sdkEnabled->true and triggers token fetch + connect. There is no effect that republishes the mic track when session later becomes non-null. SDK does not auto-republish on connect.\n  implication: Whichever track is enabled FIRST is never published to the SFU. If mic is enabled before camera (natural for \"voice\"), the audio producer is never created -> remote never receives audio. This matches the tested scenario where the remote DID see camera video (camera enabled second, session present -> publishCamera succeeded) but heard no audio. Secondary, order-dependent defect on the produce side. Silent (no throw) — consistent with \"no errors reported\".\n\n- timestamp: 2026-06-28\n  checked: grep for audio playback wiring across src/features/{room,media,voice}\n  found: The ONLY HTMLAudioElement / srcObject / .play() for audio lives in the LEGACY P2P path use-voice-chat.ts (lines 119, 168, 175-196) — it creates per-user `<audio>` elements, sets srcObject, and calls play() with autoplay-block handling. The SFU path (use-media.ts -> VideoChatGrid) has no equivalent.\n  implication: The SFU rewrite reproduced the VIDEO srcObject wiring but omitted the AUDIO element wiring that the proven legacy path had. Confirms the audio-attach omission is the root cause, not an environmental/SFU issue.\n\n## Resolution\n\nroot_cause: |\n  PRIMARY (unconditional, suspect #2): On the SFU path the remote audio track is consumed correctly by the SDK and surfaced as `remoteParticipants[].audioTrack`, but it is never attached to any audible DOM element. VideoChatGrid's VideoTile is passed `audioTrack` (VideoChatGrid.tsx:96) but never reads it (destructure at 132-140 omits it); the only media element is a `<video>` whose srcObject is a video-ONLY stream (`new MediaStream([videoTrack])`, line 152), and when the camera is off no element renders at all. There is no `<audio autoPlay>` element anywhere on the SFU path. The legacy P2P path (use-voice-chat.ts) does this correctly with HTMLAudioElement+srcObject+play(); the SFU rewrite omitted it. Result: audio is delivered to the browser but never played.\n\n  SECONDARY (order-dependent, suspect #1): use-media.ts enableMic publishes the mic track only `if (session)` (line 260), but on the first enable `session` is null (sdkEnabled is still false until setIsMicActive flips it), so publishMic is skipped and never retried (no republish-on-connect effect; SDK does not auto-republish). When mic is enabled before the camera, the audio producer is never created — the remote receives no audio at all. In the tested scenario (remote saw camera but heard nothing) the camera was enabled second with a live session, so video published while the first-enabled mic did not.\n\n  Suspect #4 (SFU codec/transport reject) and #3 (autoplay-block) are refuted (see Eliminated): no errors reported and no audio element exists to be blocked.\nfix: |\n  (not applied — find_root_cause_only mode)\n  Direction: (1) In VideoChatGrid/VideoTile, attach the remote audioTrack to an audible element — render a dedicated `<audio autoPlay playsInline>` per remote participant (NOT muted, NOT local) whose srcObject is `new MediaStream([audioTrack])`, decoupled from the camera-off branch so audio plays even when video is off; mirror the legacy use-voice-chat.ts play()/autoplay-block handling. (2) In use-media.ts, decouple publishing from the enable closure's `session`: add an effect that publishes any active local mic/camera tracks whenever `session` transitions to non-null (and on (re)connect), so a track enabled before the session exists is still published.\nverification: |\n  (not applied — find_root_cause_only)\nfiles_changed: []\n"
