    "found": "aiohttp calls pass timeout=600 (bounded 10 min, raise -> caught by poll loop). Every `requests` call in RhubClient has NO timeout: can_info (rhub_cli.py:80), publish_log (rhub_cli.py:106), and others. publish_logs() calls cli.publish_log() for every queued redis \"logs\" entry; logs are pushed by the task_runner itself (add_log on every poll exception) AND by pacs/deid/reid/router containers (dcm_listener.py, deid.py, dcm_router.py call add_log ~50 times).",
    "implication": "A single requests.post to /rtoh/logs that never gets a response (connection established, request sent, network drops / middlebox loses state, no RST reaches the CAN, no TCP keepalive) blocks forever. Because publish_logs() runs synchronously inside start() on the event-loop thread, that one hung socket read freezes the polling task too -> no GET /ctoh/task ever again -> no \"heartbeat\", results stay pending, and no further log lines (matches CAN 25: errors only on Sep 11, then silence).",
