    "checked": "LIVE test against the real pyeicon hub 1.0.12 on deid (100.91.242.40:5003, tailscale). Local CAN = edgecan:dev image (aiohttp 3.9.4, requests 2.31.0, py 3.11.16) with the tarball tree mounted at /tmp/pyedge, instance 44 (TestNoah) token, POLL_INTERVAL=10, 1 synthetic log/s pushed to redis \"logs\" (stand-in for ingest). CAN -> faultproxy -> hub. Fault \"inflight\": a POST /rtoh/logs is delivered to the hub, its response swallowed, the CAN socket frozen forever (no FIN/RST), all open conns frozen, new conns refused for 20s, then restored. Fault \"ws_fail\": first GET /ctoh/workstations at start gets a 502. After restore a harmless pending can_task (queue NetTest, worker builtins.print) is inserted for instance 44; pickup = hub status pending -> queued. Hub-side counts from Caddy ingress.log filtered by CAN 44's X-Can-Key. Scripts/results: session scratchpad live/{faultproxy.py,run_live.sh,analyze.py,runs/}.",
    "found": "(hub-side /ctoh/task counts; post window 90s)\npristine 1.13.10 inflight: polls pre 2 / post 0; log posts post 0; task 178 stayed pending; llen 4 -> 119. Main thread stack: rhub_cli.py:106 <- tasks.py:77 <- task_runner.py:177 start <- :206 main. FIELD SYMPTOM REPRODUCED ON THE REAL HUB.\npatched  1.13.10 inflight: polls resume +5.8s after restore (9 post); log posts resume +10.1s (124 post); task 179 queued ~12s after insert; llen 34 -> 1. \"Read timed out (read timeout=30)\" exactly 30.0s after the drop. Main thread idle in the selector at the end.\npristine 1.15.6  inflight: polls resume +6.2s (poller survives) but log posts after restore 0; llen 10 -> 129 growing (cause 3 confirmed live).\npatched  1.15.6  inflight: polls +6.6s; log posts +10.1s (125); task 181 queued; llen end 4.\npristine 1.15.6  ws_fail: 0 /ctoh/task for 90s while 91 log posts flowed; \"Task exception was never retrieved\"; task 182 stayed pending (cause 2 confirmed live).\npatched  1.15.6  ws_fail: \"Failed to fetch workstations, polling for tasks anyway\"; 9 polls; task 183 queued.\nExtra finding (no fault): pristine 1.13.10 with 2 logs/s (~0.4s per hub log POST over tailscale) made only 1 /ctoh/task poll in 25s - the synchronous publish_logs drain starves the poller under log load alone. A2 (executor offload) fixes this too.",
    "implication": "Fix verified end-to-end against the real hub with the prod dependency versions. Remaining human step: field confirmation on a customer-type CAN (or accept this run) -> archive.",
